  "id": 9,
  "title": "Body & health",
  "goal": "Name parts of the body, say what's wrong when you're ill, understand a doctor's advice and give simple advice yourself.",
  "intro": "When you're ill in Nepali, illnesses *come to you* or *strike you*: **मलाई ज्वरो आयो** 'a fever came to me', **मलाई रुघा लाग्यो** 'a cold struck me'. A part of your body *hurts by itself*: **मेरो टाउको दुख्यो** 'my head hurt'. This builds on the मलाई construction from unit 5.\n\nYou'll also learn to say what someone **should** or **shouldn't** do — handy for following a doctor's or a pharmacist's instructions.",
