  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Saying what's wrong",
      "body": "Nepali describes illness as something that happens **to** you. Three patterns cover almost everything:\n\n**1. मलाई + illness + आयो / लाग्यो** — 'X came / struck to me':\nमलाई ज्वरो **आयो** (fever) · मलाई रुघा **लाग्यो** (cold) · खोकी लाग्यो (cough) · पखाला लाग्यो (diarrhoea) · वाकवाकी लाग्यो (nausea) · चोट लाग्यो (injury).\n\n**2. मेरो + body part + दुख्यो / दुख्छ** — 'my X hurts': मेरो टाउको दुख्यो 'I have a headache', मेरो दाँत दुख्छ 'my tooth hurts'. Use the progressive दुखिरहेको छ for 'is hurting right now'.\n\n**3. म बिरामी छु** — 'I am ill', or **मलाई सन्चो छैन** 'I'm not well'.\n\nThe doctor's question is **के भयो?** 'What happened?' or **के समस्या छ?** 'What's the problem?'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "मेरो छोरालाई ज्वरो आयो।", "roman": "mero chhorālāi jwaro āyo.", "en": "My son has a fever." },
        { "native": "उनलाई रुघाखोकी लागेको छ।", "roman": "unlāi rughākhoki lāgeko chha.", "en": "She has a cold and a cough." },
        { "native": "मेरो ढाड दुखिरहेको छ।", "roman": "mero ḍhāḍ dukhiraheko chha.", "en": "My back is aching." },
        { "native": "खुट्टामा चोट लाग्यो।", "roman": "khuṭṭāmā choṭ lāgyo.", "en": "I hurt my leg." },
        { "native": "बच्चा बिरामी छ।", "roman": "bachchā birāmi chha.", "en": "The child is ill." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "'Should' and 'shouldn't'",
      "body": "**-नुपर्छ** (verb stem + नु + पर्छ, lit. 'it falls to do') means 'must / need to / should': **आराम गर्नुपर्छ** 'you should rest'. The doer can take **-ले**: तपाईंले… (unit 16 explains ले fully) or **-लाई**: तपाईंलाई अस्पताल जानुपर्छ.\n\n**-नुहुँदैन** means 'must not / shouldn't' (lit. 'it doesn't do to'): चिसो पानी **खानुहुँदैन** 'you shouldn't drink cold water'.\n\nA gentler suggestion: **[verb]-ए हुन्छ** 'it'd be fine to / you could': औषधि खाए हुन्छ 'you could take some medicine'. And **-नु राम्रो** 'it's better to'.",
      "examples": [
        { "native": "तपाईंले धेरै पानी खानुपर्छ।", "roman": "tapāiṃle dherai pāni khānuparchha.", "en": "You should drink lots of water." },
        { "native": "मलाई डाक्टरकहाँ जानुपर्छ।", "roman": "malāi ḍākṭarkahāṃ jānuparchha.", "en": "I need to go to the doctor." },
        { "native": "बिरामी हुँदा काममा जानुहुँदैन।", "roman": "birāmi huṃdā kāmmā jānuhuṃdaina.", "en": "You shouldn't go to work when you're ill." },
        { "native": "आज आराम गरे हुन्छ।", "roman": "āja ārām gare hunchha.", "en": "You could take a rest today." },
        { "native": "बिहान जाँच गराउनु राम्रो।", "roman": "bihāna jāṃch garāunu rāmro.", "en": "It's better to get a check-up in the morning." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "dialogue": {
    "title": "At the clinic",
    "setting": "Tom feels ill after eating street food and goes to a small clinic in Thamel.",
    "lines": [
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "बस्नुहोस्। तपाईंलाई के भयो?", "roman": "basnuhos. tapāiṃlāi ke bhayo?", "en": "Please sit down. What's the matter?" },
      { "speaker": "Tom", "native": "हिजो रातिदेखि मलाई ज्वरो आएको छ।", "roman": "hijo rātidekhi malāi jwaro āeko chha.", "en": "I've had a fever since last night." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "अरू के समस्या छ?", "roman": "aru ke samasyā chha?", "en": "Any other problems?" },
      { "speaker": "Tom", "native": "टाउको दुख्छ, अनि पेट पनि दुख्छ।", "roman": "ṭāuko dukhchha, ani peṭ pani dukhchha.", "en": "My head aches, and my stomach hurts too." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "पखाला लागेको छ?", "roman": "pakhālā lāgeko chha?", "en": "Do you have diarrhoea?" },
      { "speaker": "Tom", "native": "अलिअलि। वाकवाकी पनि लाग्छ।", "roman": "aliali. bākbāki pani lāgchha.", "en": "A little. I feel nauseous too." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "हिजो के खानुभयो?", "roman": "hijo ke khānubhayo?", "en": "What did you eat yesterday?" },
      { "speaker": "Tom", "native": "बाटोमा पानीपुरी खाएँ।", "roman": "bāṭomā pānipuri khāeṃ.", "en": "I had panipuri on the street." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "त्यसैले होला। यो औषधि दिनको दुई पटक खानुहोस्, र उमालेको पानी मात्र खानुहोस्।", "roman": "tyasaile holā. yo ausadhi dinko dui paṭak khānuhos, ra umāleko pāni mātra khānuhos.", "en": "That'll be why. Take this medicine twice a day, and drink only boiled water." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "दुई दिन आराम गर्नुपर्छ।", "roman": "dui din ārām garnuparchha.", "en": "You need to rest for two days." },
      { "speaker": "Tom", "native": "धन्यवाद, डाक्टर साब।", "roman": "dhanyabād, ḍākṭar sāb.", "en": "Thank you, doctor." },
      { "speaker": "Doctor", "native": "चाँडै निको हुनुहोस्!", "roman": "chāṃḍai niko hunuhos!", "en": "Get well soon!" }
    ]
  },
  "culture": "In the mountains, altitude sickness is called **लेक लाग्नु** *lek lāgnu* 'the high hills strike you' — guides will tell you बिस्तारै, बिस्तारै 'slowly, slowly' and to drink lots of water and garlic soup. Many medicines can be bought over the counter at an **औषधि पसल**, and the pharmacist often acts as a first doctor. Alongside modern medicine, many Nepalis also use Ayurveda, home remedies (hot water, turmeric, ginger) and, in villages, traditional healers (**धामी-झाँक्री**).",
  "lessons": [
